\newlabel{fig:horizon}{{2}{5}{$\netload $ observability ratio vs.\ horizon length for building~1. Short horizons ($h \leq 8$) have no price variation, so the battery is unused and $\netload = z^*$ (trivially observable). At $h=16$, the price change activates the battery and observability degrades sharply. Longer horizons ($h=32$) provide more data, slightly improving observability}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:horizon@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][3][]5}{}{}{}}
